# Recipient of every settled payment. Published in plain sight in each 402
# challenge, so it is an advertised address with a public balance: give it its own
# key, and never the key that controls a name or a treasury.
# Unset, the route answers 503. It does not become free.
X402_PAY_TO=

# CAIP-2 network. Base Sepolia by default. There is no localhost option because a
# facilitator cannot verify or settle against a local chain.
X402_NETWORK=eip155:84532

# The testnet facilitator is free and needs no signup.
X402_FACILITATOR_URL=https://x402.org/facilitator

# Price per read. Dollar syntax means USDC.
#
# The backslash is not decoration. Next's env loader expands `$0` as a variable, so
# `X402_PRICE=$0.50` in `.env.local` loads as `.50` and the paid route answers 500
# with `Invalid money format: .50`, which names nothing a reader could act on.
# Single quotes do not stop it; the backslash does.
X402_PRICE=\$0.01

# Where the windows come from. A directory, a comma separated list, or one file.
# A directory is read shallow and only its .jsonl files are taken, so a README or a
# sidecar beside them is not parsed as windows. Each file may have a <name>.day
# sidecar holding one ISO date, which is the day the footage belongs to; without one
# the day comes from producedAt, which is the detector's clock and moves if it is
# re-run. The board is built from these files, per day and per species.
WINDOWS_SNAPSHOT=fixtures/windows.synthetic.jsonl

# Comma separated aliases that must not leave the building. Read at runtime and
# never committed: the list is specimen data, and writing it into this repository
# would publish the thing it protects. A window touching any of these is dropped
# whole rather than redacted.
EMBARGOED_ALIASES=

# The agent's own key. It pays for reads and signs nothing else, and EIP-3009 signing
# touches no chain, so it needs an RPC for nothing. Its address is also what --agent
# stamps on the ingest credential, which makes it an attribution identity as well as a
# spending key. It must never be the address in X402_PAY_TO: a payment from an address
# to itself settles without complaint, proves nothing, and puts two identical addresses
# in the one screenshot a demo needs most.
AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Ceiling per payment. The library default is a dollar and a window costs a cent, so
# this is never reached. It is set anyway, because the price arrives from the server in
# the challenge and a client that pays whatever it is told is one typo from paying it.
# Escaped for the same reason as X402_PRICE above.
AGENT_MAX_PER_PAYMENT=\$1.00

# The paid window endpoint. Used only when AGENT_ENS_NAME is unset: setting a name
# does not make this a fallback, it makes this unused, because a name that resolves
# to nothing is not permission to read from somewhere else.
WINDOWS_URL=

# An ENS name whose x402:windows record holds the endpoint. Optional. When set, the
# record is read at every run and must name an https url, so the operator can move
# the endpoint without shipping the agent again. Nothing is registered yet.
AGENT_ENS_NAME=
AGENT_ENS_RPC_URL=

# The name Zenbit has issued to THIS agent, checked against the payer at startup.
# Optional; unset means the agent claims no name. Set means the claim has to hold: if
# the name's address record is missing or names another address the agent refuses to
# start, because the proposals it writes would carry an identity this key cannot
# substantiate. Different job from AGENT_ENS_NAME above, which holds the endpoint
# record and belongs to the service rather than to any one agent.
#
# Zenbit issues these and the agent does not own them: a subname's records live in the
# parent's resolver and only the parent's owner writes them.
AGENT_IDENTITY_NAME=

# Where the agent proposes clips, and the credential it proposes with. The key is a
# bearer, so it is sent in a header on every request: this url must be https, or the
# credential travels in clear text to whoever is listening. The key is shown once at
# mint time and cannot be recovered.
XOVI_INGEST_URL=
XOVI_INGEST_KEY=

# The one wallet the credential above belongs to. Every other wallet proposes with
# the credential minted for it at enrolment, or not at all: with this unset the
# environment holds a credential for nobody, and a run under any wallet without
# one stops at the honest step rather than proposing as somebody else.
XOVI_INGEST_KEY_PAYER=

# Minting credentials for enrolled wallets, on the reviewing application. The
# secret is a bearer sent to POST /api/ingest/keys at the ingest url's origin and
# to nothing else; it is read in one function and never returned or logged. The
# credential that comes back is answered once by the other side, so it is stored
# at rest under the key below, AES-256-GCM, thirty two random bytes as hex. Losing
# the key orphans every stored credential and the other side will not answer them
# again; rotate by re-minting. Neither value is ever a NEXT_PUBLIC one.
INGEST_MINT_SECRET=
CREDENTIAL_KEY=

# Windows a person has already refused, so the agent stops asking. Defaults to
# .agent-ledger.json in the working directory. It quotes the refusal text the server
# returned, so it is gitignored rather than committed.
AGENT_LEDGER=

# The proof of human registry, and the chain it is read on. Read World Chain, chain
# 480, because that is the only chain the registration tool writes: the published
# version rejects a network flag whatever its README says. The same contract is
# deployed at the same address on Base Sepolia with separate state, so pointing this
# at the payment chain returns zero for every agent, the cap fails closed and every
# read settles while looking exactly like a world where nobody registered.
#
# Note what that means: payments settle on Base Sepolia and this read happens on a
# mainnet. It moves nothing, holds nothing and needs no key, but the narration must
# not say testnet without qualifying it.
AGENTBOOK_ADDRESS=
AGENTBOOK_RPC_URL=

# Free reads per verified human per UTC day. Twenty by default. Zero is a valid
# count rather than a missing one, and it is the switch that lets the paid read be
# demonstrated by a payer who is registered: with the cap at zero their reads settle
# and produce the explorer transaction the paid leg needs.
HUMAN_FREE_READS_PER_DAY=

# Where the count and the receipts live. Unset, there is no allowance and every read
# settles, which is what this endpoint did before the cap existed. That is the
# correct degradation and not a stub, and it means the free path cannot be shown
# until this is set.
DATABASE_URL=

# Server secret used to derive what the usage table stores, so that a copy of that
# table on its own cannot be matched against on chain registrations. Thirty two
# random bytes as hex. It is a secret held outside this repository and it is never
# committed: losing it orphans the counters and nothing else, since nothing else is
# keyed on it and the underlying value stays readable on chain either way.
# Unset, there is no derivation, so there is no allowance and every read settles.
HUMAN_ID_KEY=

# The chain this milestone anchors to, and the key that signs the attestations.
# Ethereum Sepolia and nothing else: the scripts refuse any other chain unless an
# explicit flag is passed, because a script that writes to whatever chain the
# environment points at is how a definition lands somewhere nobody chose.
#
# The signing key is read from a file on the operator's machine for the demo and is
# NOT added to the hosting environment. It is the schema registrar as well as the
# attester, and it is not the agent's payer, not the recipient of payments and not
# the controller of any name.
ANCHOR_RPC_URL=
ATTESTATION_PRIVATE_KEY=

# The reviewing application's public list of confirmed clips. Unauthenticated,
# takes no parameters, and is read rather than pushed from, which is why anchoring
# needs no change on that side.
XOVI_CLIPS_URL=

# The same list, read by the deployed page rather than by the anchoring tool on an
# operator's machine, which is why it is a second variable and not a reuse: the two
# readers are different processes and may point at different deployments. Unset, the
# proposals route refuses rather than guessing an origin, because a default here is
# how a deployment ends up reading a list nobody chose. That list serves CONFIRMED
# rows only, so the section it feeds can show confirmed proposals and nothing else.
XOVI_PUBLIC_URL=

# The deployed index the paid query reads. Unset, the query tool refuses to build
# rather than answering an empty list, because an empty list is a real answer
# meaning nothing has been anchored and a missing url is a misconfiguration.
SUBGRAPH_URL=

# Nothing new is needed for the networked query: it reads the same X402_PAY_TO,
# X402_NETWORK, X402_PRICE, SUBGRAPH_URL and ANCHOR_RPC_URL the local one does, and
# holds no session, so the route needs no state of its own.

# Enrollment with World ID from the page, the second source of a person behind a
# wallet beside AgentBook. The three public values are read by the widget in the
# page AND by the server, which signs with the same action and checks a result
# against the same environment, so there is one value for each and nothing to
# drift. The environment must match the action created in the developer portal
# and the app the person holds: `staging` verifies against the simulator at
# simulator.worldcoin.org and nothing else, `production` against World App and
# nothing else, and a mismatch produces no result and looks like a broken page.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WORLD_APP_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_WORLD_ACTION=enrol-agent
NEXT_PUBLIC_WORLD_ENVIRONMENT=staging

# The relying party the server forwards results to, and the key it signs every
# request with. The key is server only: it authenticates this relying party to
# World, so a key in the page would let anyone open requests in Zenbit's name. It
# is read in one function, used for one signature, never returned and never
# logged, and a check walks every client file for its name. The portal shows it
# once; a lost key is rotated, not recovered. Thirty two bytes as hex.
WORLD_RP_ID=
WORLD_SIGNING_KEY=
